	<entry>
		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Réponse à&#160;:  audit table with integer column]]></title>
		<link rel="alternate" href="http://forums.postgresql.fr/viewtopic.php?pid=23693#p23693"/>
		<content type="html"><![CDATA[<p>Finaly, i&#039;m not sure the problem was do to CONCAT ignoring NULL argument but to the fact that in the CASE WHEN i was returning either an integer &#039;NEW.&quot;categorySignId&quot; or varchar &#039;NULL&#039;.<br />Following syntax works perfectly:<br />INSERT INTO audit (stamp,query) VALUES( now(), CONCAT(&#039;INSERT INTO proposition VALUES(&#039;,NEW.id,&#039;,&#039;,quote_nullable(NEW.text),&#039;,&#039;,CASE WHEN quote_nullable(NEW.&quot;categorySignId&quot;) IS NULL THEN &#039;NULL&#039; ELSE NEW.&quot;categorySignId&quot; END,&#039;);&#039;))</p><p>Is there any risk with an insert query which would looks like: INSERT INTO proposition VALUES(1,&#039;Exemple&#039;,&#039;1&#039;);<br />While third parameter is an integer?</p>]]></content>
